@@ -47,3 +47,10 @@
 - [ ] `internal/notification/slow_upstream.go:slowUpstreamSummary` is a fourth per-request-type `switch`. Include it in the per-type table planned in the second-pass entry above.
 - [ ] `internal/notification/slow_upstream.go`: the `SlowUpstreamNotifier` doc gives the caller's reason (pinentry context), which `internal/proxy/slow_upstream.go:23` also states. The `NotifySlowUpstream` doc lists the body contents, which `formatSlowUpstreamBody` owns. Cut both down to the item's own contract.
 - [ ] `internal/notification/desktop.go:146` reads the D-Bus signal body by position (`sig.Body[0]`, `sig.Body[1]`). The `NotifyPersistent` doc names the D-Bus method `CloseNotification`, and "alternating (id, label) pairs" is stated at both `:30` and `:190`. Decode the signal into a named struct and give each fact one owner.
+
+## Unsmell run 2026-11-01 (fourth pass): markup escaping follow-ups
+
+- [ ] `internal/notification/markup.go:text` escapes `&`, `<` and `>` but lets `\n` through, and both bodies (`body.go:bodyBuilder.processChain`, `slow_upstream.go:formatSlowUpstreamBody`) use `\n` as their line separator. A label or process name with a newline can fake an extra body line, such as a spoofed process-chain line. Give `markup` a `newline()` method for structural breaks, and have `text` replace newlines in untrusted text. This changes what notifications show.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/body.go:formatBody` treats `req.Items[0]` as "the SSH key" of an SSH sign request by position. `approval.Request` does not say so. Give the request a named accessor (or a typed SSH field) next to the planned `"destination"` constant.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/body.go:formatBody`: a GPG request with a nil `GPGSignInfo` returns an empty body and drops the process chain, while an SSH request with no items still shows the chain. Decide whether the chain should always be shown.
+- [ ] `internal/notification/slow_upstream.go:11`: the `persistentNotifier` doc lists its two methods ("sends … and can dismiss them"). Rewrite it as the seam's place: what the slow-upstream notifier needs from `DBusNotifier`, so tests can replace it.
